                    </p>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     SIMPLE EXPLANATION
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Simple Explanation
                </h2>

                <div class="concept-box">

                    <p class="section-text mb-0">

                        Think of an <strong>Array</strong> like a box
                        containing multiple values.

                        <br /><br />

                        For example, one Array can contain multiple course
                        names, numbers, student names, or other values.

                        <br /><br />

                        A <strong>String</strong> is used to store text.
                        For example:

                        <strong>
                            "JavaScript"
                        </strong>

                        can be stored inside a String variable.

                        <br /><br />

                        JavaScript provides many built-in properties and
                        methods to work with both Arrays and Strings.

                    </p>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     ARRAYS
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    What is an Array?
                </h2>

                <p class="section-text">

                    An Array is a collection of values stored in a single
                    variable. Each value has an index, and Array indexing
                    starts from <strong>0</strong>.

                </p>


                <div class="code-box">

<pre><code>const courses = [
    "Java",
    ".NET",
    "Python",
    "JavaScript"
];</code></pre>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     STRINGS
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    What is a String?
                </h2>

                <p class="section-text">

                    A String represents text in JavaScript. Strings can
                    contain letters, numbers, spaces, and special
                    characters.

                </p>


                <div class="code-box">

<pre><code>const courseName = "JavaScript Full Stack";</code></pre>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     PARTS
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Arrays &amp; Strings at a Glance
                </h2>


                <div class="part-card">

                    <span class="part-number">
                        1
                    </span>

                    <strong>
                        Array
                    </strong>

                    <p class="section-text mt-2 mb-0">

                        Used to store multiple values inside one
                        collection.

                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="part-card">

                    <span class="part-number">
                        2
                    </span>

                    <strong>
                        Index
                    </strong>

                    <p class="section-text mt-2 mb-0">

                        Array elements are accessed using indexes.
                        The first index is <strong>0</strong>.

                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="part-card">

                    <span class="part-number">
                        3
                    </span>

                    <strong>
                        String
                    </strong>

                    <p class="section-text mt-2 mb-0">

                        Used to store and manipulate text.

                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="part-card">

                    <span class="part-number">
                        4
                    </span>

                    <strong>
                        Methods
                    </strong>

                    <p class="section-text mt-2 mb-0">

                        JavaScript provides methods to add, remove,
                        search, modify, and process Array and String data.

                    </p>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     DIAGRAM
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Arrays &amp; Strings Flow
                </h2>

                <div class="diagram-box">

                    <div class="diagram-title">
                        How JavaScript Handles Collections and Text
                    </div>

                    <div class="data-flow">

                        <div class="diagram-item">

                            Data

                            <br />

                            <small>
                                Values / Text
                            </small>

                        </div>


                        <div class="diagram-arrow">
                            →
                        </div>


                        <div class="diagram-item diagram-highlight">

                            Array / String

                            <br />

                            <small>
                                Store Data
                            </small>

                        </div>


                        <div class="diagram-arrow">
                            →
                        </div>


                        <div class="diagram-item">

                            Properties

                            <br />

                            <small>
                                length
                            </small>

                        </div>


                        <div class="diagram-arrow">
                            →
                        </div>


                        <div class="diagram-item">

                            Methods

                            <br />

                            <small>
                                Process Data
                            </small>

                        </div>


                        <div class="diagram-arrow">
                            →
                        </div>


                        <div class="diagram-item">

                            Result

                            <br />

                            <small>
                                Output
                            </small>

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     EXAMPLE 1
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Example 1: Creating an Array
                </h2>

                <p class="section-text">

                    We can create an Array using square brackets
                    <strong>[]</strong>.

                </p>


                <div class="code-box">

<pre><code>const courses = [
    "Java",
    ".NET",
    "Python",
    "JavaScript"
];

console.log(courses);</code></pre>

                </div>


                <div class="try-it-container">

                    <button type="button"
                            class="try-it-btn"
                            onclick="runArraysStringsExample1()">

                        ▶ Try It

                    </button>

                </div>


                <div class="output-box">

                    <strong>
                        Output:
                    </strong>

                    <br />

                    Java, .NET, Python, JavaScript

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     EXAMPLE 2
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Example 2: Accessing Array Elements
                </h2>

                <p class="section-text">

                    Array elements can be accessed using their index.
                    Remember that Array indexing starts from 0.

                </p>


                <div class="code-box">

<pre><code>const courses = [
    "Java",
    ".NET",
    "Python",
    "JavaScript"
];

console.log(courses[0]);
console.log(courses[2]);</code></pre>

                </div>


                <div class="try-it-container">

                    <button type="button"
                            class="try-it-btn"
                            onclick="runArraysStringsExample2()">

                        ▶ Try It

                    </button>

                </div>


                <div class="output-box">

                    <strong>
                        Output:
                    </strong>

                    <br />

                    Java
                    <br />

                    Python

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     EXAMPLE 3
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Example 3: Working with a String
                </h2>

                <p class="section-text">

                    A String can store text, and JavaScript provides
                    properties such as <strong>length</strong> to
                    work with it.

                </p>


                <div class="code-box">

<pre><code>const courseName = "JavaScript";

console.log(courseName);
console.log(courseName.length);</code></pre>

                </div>


                <div class="try-it-container">

                    <button type="button"
                            class="try-it-btn"
                            onclick="runArraysStringsExample3()">

                        ▶ Try It

                    </button>

                </div>


                <div class="output-box">

                    <strong>
                        Output:
                    </strong>

                    <br />

                    JavaScript
                    <br />

                    10

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     EXAMPLE 4
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    Example 4: Array and String Together
                </h2>

                <p class="section-text">

                    Arrays can store multiple Strings. This is commonly
                    used when working with collections of names, courses,
                    products, or other text values.

                </p>


                <div class="code-box">

<pre><code>const students = [
    "Rahul",
    "Sneha",
    "Amit"
];

console.log("First Student:", students[0]);
console.log("Total Students:", students.length);</code></pre>

                </div>


                <div class="try-it-container">

                    <button type="button"
                            class="try-it-btn"
                            onclick="runArraysStringsExample4()">

                        ▶ Try It

                    </button>

                </div>


                <div class="output-box">

                    <strong>
                        Output:
                    </strong>

                    <br />

                    First Student: Rahul
                    <br />

                    Total Students: 3

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     IMPORTANT NOTE
                     ================================================= -->

                <div class="note-box">

                    <strong>
                        Important Note:
                    </strong>

                    <p class="section-text mb-0 mt-2">

                        JavaScript Array indexes start from
                        <strong>0</strong>.

                        <br /><br />

                        For example, in:

                        <strong>
                            ["Java", ".NET", "Python"]
                        </strong>

                        <br />

                        Java has index <strong>0</strong>,
                        .NET has index <strong>1</strong>,
                        and Python has index <strong>2</strong>.

                    </p>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     WHAT WE WILL LEARN NEXT
                     ================================================= -->

                <h2 class="section-title">
                    What We Will Learn Next
                </h2>

                <div class="concept-box">

                    <p class="section-text mb-0">

                        In the next topics, we will learn Arrays and
                        Strings in more detail.

                        <br /><br />

                        <strong>Arrays</strong> →
                        Array creation, indexing, updating, and
                        Array Methods.

                        <br /><br />

                        <strong>Strings</strong> →
                        String creation, indexing, properties, and
                        String Methods.

                    </p>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     SUMMARY
                     ================================================= -->

                <div class="summary-box">

                    <h2>
                        Summary
                    </h2>

                    <p>

                        Arrays are used to store multiple values in a
                        single collection, while Strings are used to
                        store and work with text. JavaScript provides
                        indexes, properties, and built-in methods to
                        access and process Array and String data.
                        In the upcoming topics, we will explore Arrays,
                        Array Methods, Strings, and String Methods in
                        detail.

                    </p>

                </div>


                <!-- =================================================
                     PREVIOUS / NEXT
                     ================================================= -->

                <div class="bottom-navigation">

                    <a href="@Url.Action("CallbackFunctions", "Functions", new { area = "JavaScript" })"
                       class="nav-btn previous-btn">

                        ← Previous: Callback Functions

                    </a>


                    <a href="@Url.Action("Arrays", "ArraysStrings", new { area = "JavaScript" })"
                       class="nav-btn next-btn">

                        Next: Arrays →

                    </a>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>

    </div>

</main>


<!-- =========================================================
     TRY IT JAVASCRIPT
     ========================================================= -->

<script>

    function openCompiler(code) {

        const compilerUrl =
            '/JavaScriptCompiler/Index?code=' +
            encodeURIComponent(code);

        window.open(
            compilerUrl,
            '_blank'
        );
    }


    // ========================================================
    // EXAMPLE 1
    // ========================================================

    function runArraysStringsExample1() {

        const code = `
const courses = [
    "Java",
    ".NET",
    "Python",
    "JavaScript"
];

console.log(courses);
`;

        openCompiler(code);
    }


    // ========================================================
    // EXAMPLE 2
    // ========================================================

    function runArraysStringsExample2() {

        const code = `
const courses = [
    "Java",
    ".NET",
    "Python",
    "JavaScript"
];

console.log(courses[0]);
console.log(courses[2]);
`;

        openCompiler(code);
    }


    // ========================================================
    // EXAMPLE 3
    // ========================================================

    function runArraysStringsExample3() {

        const code = `
const courseName = "JavaScript";

console.log(courseName);
console.log(courseName.length);
`;

        openCompiler(code);
    }


    // ========================================================
    // EXAMPLE 4
    // ========================================================

    function runArraysStringsExample4() {

        const code = `
const students = [
    "Rahul",
    "Sneha",
    "Amit"
];

console.log("First Student:", students[0]);
console.log("Total Students:", students.length);
`;

        openCompiler(code);
    }

</script>